  "id": "decisional-balance",
  "term": "decisional balance",
  "definition": "Decisional balance is the mental process of comparing the expected benefits and drawbacks of continuing a behavior versus stopping it. In behavior change contexts, it refers to how a person weighs possible gains, losses, self-approval, and effects on important others when deciding whether to change.",
